---
// Mission, variant C: "Two column with pull quotes".
// Tightened thesis prose on the left, two margin notes on the right. The
// notes column sits beside the prose from 900px up and stacks beneath it
// below that. Both quotes are verbatim from the linked sources.
import "../../styles/variants/mission.css";
---

<section class="py-20 sm:py-28 border-t border-rule">
  <div class="reveal max-w-[1000px] mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-6">Mission</div>

    <div class="mission-grid">
      <div class="mission-prose">
        <p>
          <span class="mission-lede"
            >Every agent client re-implements every integration.</span
          > The same API is wired up again for each client, with its own auth and
          its own failure modes. Credentials get pasted in five places. No client
          shares an idea of what a tool may do.<a
            class="mission-ref"
            href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/code-execution-with-mcp"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            aria-label="Reference 1">1</a
          >
        </p>

        <p>
          Executor gives every tool one shape. A name, an input schema, an
          output schema. MCP, OpenAPI, or GraphQL, it makes no difference: any
          agent calls any of them the same way. Tools should belong to you, not
          to one client or one model provider.<a
            class="mission-ref"
            href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/code-mode/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            aria-label="Reference 2">2</a
          >
        </p>

        <p>
          The safe path has to be the easy path. Executor keeps the semantics it
          imported: GET against DELETE, destructiveHint, GraphQL mutations.<a
            class="mission-ref"
            href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            aria-label="Reference 3">3</a
          > Calls run in a sandbox. Credentials are attached host-side, so a raw token
          never reaches the model.<a
            class="mission-ref"
            href="https://executor.sh/docs"
            aria-label="Reference 4">4</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="mission-notes">
        <div class="mission-note">
          <div class="mission-note__n">Note 01</div>
          <blockquote class="mission-note__quote">
            &ldquo;Tool descriptions occupy more context window space,
            increasing response time and costs.&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          <div class="mission-note__attr">
            Anthropic, <a
              href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/code-execution-with-mcp"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Code execution with MCP</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mission-note">
          <div class="mission-note__n">Note 02</div>
          <blockquote class="mission-note__quote">
            &ldquo;If true, the tool may perform destructive updates to its
            environment.&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          <div class="mission-note__attr">
            MCP spec, <a
              href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">destructiveHint</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="mission-refs-row">
      <span class="mission-refs-row__label">References</span>
      <span
        ><span class="mission-refs-row__n">[1]</span><a
          href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/code-execution-with-mcp"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Anthropic, Code execution with MCP</a
        ></span
      >
      <span
        ><span class="mission-refs-row__n">[2]</span><a
          href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/code-mode/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Cloudflare, Code Mode</a
        ></span
      >
      <span
        ><span class="mission-refs-row__n">[3]</span><a
          href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">MCP spec, tool annotations</a
        ></span
      >
      <span
        ><span class="mission-refs-row__n">[4]</span><a
          href="https://executor.sh/docs">Executor docs</a
        ></span
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
